# Templates Builder stamps

Before adding, moving, or renaming a `metadata.blockeraOne` stamp, **read
`packages/blockera-one/js/site-editor/templates-builder/STAMPS.md`** for
the full standard (grammar, uniqueness, Using stamps, catalogs, lookup,
hard-cut). Do not invent a parallel convention and do not duplicate
catalog tables here.

- Grammar: `role/id` or `role/id:variant`. Roles: `layout | section | area | container`.
- Follow **Using stamps** for which family to pick; catalogs list every id.
- Dictionary ids are globally unique on the **id token**. Nested stamps
  may still **repeat in the tree under different parents**; lookup is
  parent-scoped (`shared/stamp-lookup.ts`). Do not invent
  `loop-item-media` twins.
- Inner-region slots: `container/start`, `container/media`,
  `container/body`, `container/end`, `container/comments`. Not chrome
  `header`/`footer`. Not `content-column`. List View `metadata.name` is
  user-facing and independent of the stamp id.
- Put cross-type / engine / layout-main / page-header-family /
  posts-listing / pagination / inner-slot stamps in `shared/stamps.ts`.
- Put type-only stamps in `<type>/stamps.ts`. Promote to shared when a
  second type needs the same id — never copy.
- `wp_template` layout root is always `layout/main`. Part roots are
  `layout/site-header`, `layout/site-footer`, `layout/site-sidebar`.
- Update `STAMPS.md` in the same change as the dictionary or markup.
